    "details": "<p>Run NovaCredit, a new digital lender, and decide who gets which of four credit cards to earn the most profit. The catch: the safest customers aren't the most profitable, and good data isn't free. Start with a basic dataset and a fixed budget, cross profit thresholds to unlock exclusive data packs, and outbid rival teams before the data is gone.</p>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria:</strong></p>\n<p>Winners are decided by a published scoring formula and a panel of judges, so every result can be checked. Scoring considers:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Portfolio Profit</strong>: How much your card decisions earn on a hidden set of applicants nobody sees until the end.</li>\n<li><strong>Smart Spending</strong>: How little of your budget you needed to get there.</li>\n<li><strong>Memo</strong>: How well you justify your data purchases, and whether your lending is fair and responsible.</li>\n<li>The final reveal shows which data packs were treasure, which were traps, and who overpaid.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Team Size</strong>: 2 &ndash;4 members.</li>\n<li><strong>Duration</strong>: 3 hours.</li>\n<li><strong>Participation</strong>: Open to all college/university students of any major.</li>\n<li><strong>Tools</strong>: Python on your own laptop. No GPU needed; any library or AI assistant is allowed.</li>\n<li><strong>Kaggle account mandartory for atleast one memeber of the team</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Deliverables</strong>: A card decision for every applicant, the notebook that produced it, and a one-page memo explaining your data purchases and lending choices.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>",
